course: dictionary
lesson: 2501
title: Debris and the power of context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Debris is a noun. It means the broken pieces left behind after something has been destroyed or has fallen. Think of wood, stone and glass scattered across the ground after a storm.
explain: Read the words around the word to find its meaning. «Scientists think the Moon formed when a Mars-sized body smashed into the young Earth and threw out debris.» Smashed and threw out are the clues. Something crashed hard and flung pieces everywhere, so debris must be those broken pieces.
explain: Debris is also used in science. In space, debris is junk orbiting the Earth, such as old pieces of rockets and satellites. Notice that debris is uncountable: we say some debris, not a debris.
fact: Debris means broken pieces left after something has been destroyed or has fallen.
fact: Debris can also mean rubbish or small pieces scattered about.
fact: In science, space debris is old junk, such as pieces of rockets and satellites, orbiting the Earth.
fact: Debris is uncountable, so we do not add an s or use a or an with it.
fact: The idea that the Moon formed from debris after a huge crash is the leading idea, but it is not proven beyond doubt.
exercise: «After the storm, the beach was covered in debris.» What is debris? | *Broken bits and rubbish left behind | A tall sea wall | Wet sand and shells | Warm sunshine
exercise: «Flying debris from the crash meant everyone stayed back.» Why did people stay back? | They were lost | They wanted a picnic | They were cold | *Broken pieces could be dangerous
exercise: Space scientists track space debris. What is space debris? | Stars that have burned out | Clouds of gas near the Sun | The moons of other planets | *Old pieces of rockets and satellites orbiting Earth
test: «Please clear the debris from the path.» What does clear the debris mean? | Walk along the path | *Remove the broken bits and rubbish | Find a new path | Paint the path
test: Which phrase means junk orbiting the Earth? | Flying debris | *Space debris | Covered in debris | Clear the debris
exam: «Scientists think the Moon formed when a Mars-sized body smashed into the young Earth and threw out debris.» What does debris mean in this sentence? | A soft French cheese | A gentle wind | A bright light in the sky | *Broken pieces flung out by the crash
